## Headline: we found a train/serve skew in our own pipeline, and retracted our own conclusion

Train-time traveler features were computed as-of each trip's `start_date`, but a trip's browsing session
(the source of the labels) is dated 0-45 days *before* it, so train and validation features carried the
labels and holdout features could not: the median days since the last interaction is
**{{h_experiments.feature_skew_pre_fix.train_trips.days_since_last_interaction_median|.0f}} on train trips vs
{{h_experiments.feature_skew_pre_fix.holdout_trips.days_since_last_interaction_median|.0f}} on holdout trips**. The first tag reported the ranker as no better than content
cosine ({{h_experiments.pre_fix_headline.ndcg10_primary|.4f}} vs {{h_experiments.pre_fix_headline.ndcg10_content_cosine|.4f}}, p={{h_experiments.pre_fix_headline.wilcoxon_primary_vs_content_cosine_p|.3g}}); that
conclusion is retracted in the docs (`docs/TECHNICAL.md` sections 5.1, 10.1) and the whole pipeline was re-run.
The fix also *cost* two scorecard rows (confidence-decile Spearman
{{h_experiments.pre_fix_headline.confidence_decile_spearman|.3f}} → {{confidence_diagnosis.post_fix.decile_spearman_recomputed|.3f}}, scenario-4 flip overlap {{h_experiments.pre_fix_headline.scenario4_overlap|.3f}} → {{l_pre_scenarios.diagnostic_vs_base_jaccard|.3f}});
both were diagnosed with measured mechanisms, not tuned away. Experiment L (v1.1, below) then fixed the second in the scoring layer
({{l_pre_scenarios.diagnostic_vs_base_jaccard|.3f}} → {{scenarios.overlap_matrix.diagnostic_vs_base_jaccard|.3f}}); the first fell further ({{confidence_decile_validation.spearman_rho|.3f}}). **Holdout feature distributions were inspected
to diagnose a train/serve skew. No labels were used for selection and no hyperparameter was chosen on holdout.**

